type.description:
Describes the type of difference between `before` and `after`:
* If `MODIFIED`, then both `before` and `after` will be present, but will differ in at least one property;
* If `ADDED`, then only `after` will be present;
* If `DELETED`, then only `before` will be present.

path.description:
JSON property name(s) that must be accessed, starting from the top level of the HTTP response, to reach the
value or array needed to calculate the next offset value. Required if `operator` is "IDENTITY" or "LENGTH";
absent otherwise.

post.description:
Adds an HTTP(S) data connector to the network. Nothing is fetched from the service until the next collection;
use [Test a data connector](https://docs.fwd.app/latest/api/data-connectors/test-data-connector/) to confirm
the connector works before then.
